Z||000000||2farnorth||07-26-2001||05:44 AM||||Anyone have any ideas on how to remove the brake light switch on the Izusu 5-speed transmission.  I can get a 22 mm open end wrench part way on, but there's no room to turn it.  I don't really want to cut the wires off to use a socket.<P>thanks<P>Dave||||reg||9
Z||000001||rogergarrison||07-26-2001||06:07 AM||||the brake lite switch is mounted on the top of the brake pedal assembly. Pretty sure its same on all Fieros.||||reg||1
Z||000002||2farnorth||07-26-2001||06:13 AM||||I meant back-up light switch not brake light.<BR>sorry!||||reg||3
Z||000003||Indiana_resto_guy||07-26-2001||11:20 AM||||If you can find a deep well 22mm socket, you might be able to wad the wires up inside it. What is your problem with it? Won't work? Try pulling the plug and short the pins together (make sure the bulbs are good!) and see if they light up. If the do the switch is bad anyway cut the plug to remove!<P>Welcome to the Forum!||||reg||1
Z||000004||2farnorth||07-26-2001||01:00 PM||||I did pull the plug and when I shorted the two terminals together the lites worked, so I assumed the switch was bad.  The reason I didn't want to cut the wires is because I thought that maybe the switch  would be reparable, but I guess that won't be possible.  Once I get a new one to put in then I've got the wrench problem again unless<BR>there's some way to remove that oversize plug<BR>that's on it.<P>Thanks again<P>Dave||||reg||1
Z||000005||theogre||07-26-2001||06:52 PM||||There are sensor sockets with slots cut in the side.... You can likely buy/borrow one from many parts stores.||||reg||1
